    "title": "Significant Weight Gain and Metabolic Changes on DTG",
    "message": "Guidelines note weight gain is a problem in HIV care, particularly among women, and should be discussed proactively. The patient has gained 17 kg (BMI increased from 25.6 to 32.4 kg/m²) over 18 months since switching to a DTG-based regimen (TLD). She now has obesity, acanthosis nigricans, pre-diabetes (fasting glucose 118 mg/dL, HbA1c 6.1%), and dyslipidemia. DTG is a known contributor to weight gain. However, family history of Type 2 diabetes is a non-drug risk factor. The patient also reports increased fatigue, which aligns with metabolic syndrome.",
